Only call pthread_getname_np() on glibc and Darwin. musl lacks it
before 1.2.3 and Android bionic before API level 26, which breaks
linking the runtime for -musl/-musl1.1/-musl1.2.2 and -bionic24.
It is only used to decorate lossage messages with the thread name.

diff --git a/src/runtime/interr.c b/src/runtime/interr.c
index bf4c69b..6e405f7 100644
--- a/src/runtime/interr.c
+++ b/src/runtime/interr.c
@@ -97,7 +97,7 @@ void set_lossage_handler(void (*handler)(void))
 }
 
